    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0190" n="122" xml:id="pg122"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111/1930</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">21 April, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am glad to accept the
                    emendations suggested (except where I have run my pencil through them) and also
                    the rearrangement of paragraphs, and hasten to return the note to be copied and
                        delivered.<anchor n="25" xml:id="d117-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I took advantage of your suggestion to add the words (p. 6) “and I respectfully
                    submit that none of the circumstances urged in Your Excellency’s memorandum
                    alters the principle involved.”<anchor n="26" xml:id="d117-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>In haste,</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="25" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the note as sent, see <ref target="frus1915Supp#pg_160">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1915, supp., p.
                    160</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d117-f2" n="26" xml:id="d117-f2-content">
